# NOTE: this file is symlinked into every package that runs prettier (see
# packages/*/.prettierignore). Prettier resolves ignore files relative to the
# cwd and never searches parent directories, so a package running
# `prettier --check .` sees neither this file nor the root .gitignore unless it
# has its own copy. Two consequences:
#
#   1. every rule here has to make sense from a package root as well as from the
#      repo root, so keep the patterns path-agnostic -- `dist/`, never
#      `packages/*/dist`
#   2. prettier does read .gitignore by default, but it finds it the same way --
#      cwd only -- so the root .gitignore is invisible from a package too. Every
#      gitignored path that can show up inside a package has to be repeated
#      here, dot-prefixed ones included: `prettier --check .` walks into
#      .coverage/ and .astro/ just like any other directory.

